{"id":"h05t3","name":"Overdraft Episodes","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>transactions</b> has the columns <code>tx_id</code>, <code>account_id</code>, <code>ts</code> (timestamp), <code>amount</code> (numeric, negative for a debit) and <code>status</code>. Only transactions with the status <code>'settled'</code> change the balance; <code>'pending'</code> and <code>'failed'</code> ones are ignored.</p>\n<p>Every account starts at a balance of 0. Process the settled transactions of an account in order of <code>ts</code>, then <code>tx_id</code>, and compute the balance after each of them. An <b>overdraft episode</b> starts with a transaction after which the balance is negative while it was not negative just before (the very first transaction of an account can start an episode). The episode lasts while the balance stays negative and ends with the first transaction after which the balance is 0 or more again: that transaction is the <b>recovery</b>.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return one row per episode with the columns <code>account_id</code>, <code>started_at</code> (ts of the transaction that started it), <code>recovered_at</code> (ts of the recovery, <code>NULL</code> if the account is still negative), <code>lowest_balance</code> (the lowest balance reached during the episode) and <code>txs_in_episode</code> (number of transactions after which the balance was negative in this episode), sorted by <code>account_id</code>, then <code>started_at</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>transactions</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>tx_id</th><th>account_id</th><th>ts</th><th>amount</th><th>status</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>100</td><td>settled</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 09:00:00</td><td>-150</td><td>settled</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 09:10:00</td><td>-20</td><td>settled</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 09:20:00</td><td>300</td><td>pending</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 09:30:00</td><td>70</td><td>settled</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 09:40:00</td><td>-1</td><td>settled</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>2</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>-40</td><td>settled</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>2</td><td>2026-03-02 08:10:00</td><td>40</td><td>failed</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>2</td><td>2026-03-02 08:20:00</td><td>15</td><td>settled</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>account_id</th><th>started_at</th><th>recovered_at</th><th>lowest_balance</th><th>txs_in_episode</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 09:00:00</td><td>2026-03-02 09:30:00</td><td>-70.0</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 09:40:00</td><td>null</td><td>-1.0</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>null</td><td>-40.0</td><td>2</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>transactions</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>account_id</code>, <code>started_at</code>, <code>recovered_at</code>, <code>lowest_balance</code>, <code>txs_in_episode</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["solde cumulé","îlots","LAG avec valeur par défaut","FILTER"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>transactions</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 5 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>account_id</code>, <code>started_at</code>, <code>recovered_at</code>, <code>lowest_balance</code>, <code>txs_in_episode</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : une case vide attendue s'écrit <code>null</code> : ce n'est ni <code>0</code> ni une chaîne vide ; les dates s'affichent AAAA-MM-JJ HH:MM:SS pour une date avec heure.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 8 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"transactions":{"columns":[["tx_id","INT"],["account_id","INT"],["ts","TIMESTAMP"],["amount","NUMERIC(10,2)"],["status","TEXT"]],"rows":[[1,1,"2026-03-02 08:00:00",100,"settled"],[2,1,"2026-03-02 09:00:00",-150,"settled"],[3,1,"2026-03-02 09:10:00",-20,"settled"],[4,1,"2026-03-02 09:20:00",300,"pending"],[5,1,"2026-03-02 09:30:00",70,"settled"],[6,1,"2026-03-02 09:40:00",-1,"settled"],[7,2,"2026-03-02 08:00:00",-40,"settled"],[8,2,"2026-03-02 08:10:00",40,"failed"],[9,2,"2026-03-02 08:20:00",15,"settled"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["account_id","started_at","recovered_at","lowest_balance","txs_in_episode"],"rows":[[1,"2026-03-02 09:00:00","2026-03-02 09:30:00",-70.0,2],[1,"2026-03-02 09:40:00",null,-1.0,1],[2,"2026-03-02 08:00:00",null,-40.0,2]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"transactions":{"columns":[["tx_id","INT"],["account_id","INT"],["ts","TIMESTAMP"],["amount","NUMERIC(10,2)"],["status","TEXT"]],"rows":[[1,5,"2026-03-02 08:00:00",10,"settled"],[3,5,"2026-03-02 08:30:00",-40,"settled"],[2,5,"2026-03-02 08:30:00",25,"settled"],[4,5,"2026-03-02 08:40:00",-5,"settled"],[5,5,"2026-03-02 08:50:00",0.5,"settled"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["account_id","started_at","recovered_at","lowest_balance","txs_in_episode"],"rows":[[5,"2026-03-02 08:30:00",null,-10.0,3]]}}],"hidden_n":8,"hidden":"","solution":""}